WEBVTT

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.640
What is it like to learn AI with the AI
Confidence Academy?

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.780
It begins with being treated as someone
who has something to bring to the

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.420
conversation. Your experience, your
questions, and your judgment matter here.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.100
You do not have to arrive knowing
technical language,

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.820
and you do not have to pretend you
understand something that is still

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.680
unfamiliar. ACA was built for people who
may have looked at this space and

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.560
wondered whether there was a place for
them. There is a place to begin with a

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.540
question, to acknowledge uncertainty,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.420
and to develop understanding through
practice.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.920
Our approach is to train humans.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.800
Learning a tool is part of that, but the
purpose is to help you think clearly,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.500
participate, and make useful decisions.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.540
We want you to understand what you are
doing and why you are doing it. Imagine

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.440
working on a message you need to send.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.860
Instead of asking you to memorize a
complicated instruction,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.900
we begin with your purpose. Who is the
message for? What needs to be understood?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.780
What would a useful result look like? You
see an example, then try a conversation

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.220
yourself. When AI responds, the work
continues.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.400
You examine the message. Perhaps the tone
does not sound like you, or an important

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.960
detail is missing. You practice saying
what needs to change, then compare the

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.560
next response with what you intended.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.520
That process gives you something more
useful than a finished message. It gives

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.120
you experience directing the conversation
and recognizing whether the result serves

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.920
your purpose. The journeys provide a path
through this kind of learning.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.780
Explanations help you make sense of an
idea.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.780
Demonstrations make it visible.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.600
Guided activities give you a way to
participate.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.900
Reflection helps you notice what you
understand and where another question is

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.680
needed. An imperfect attempt is something
to examine. It can show you which

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.820
detail needs explaining,

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.880
which instruction needs adjusting, or
which answer needs checking.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:00.340
You do not have to understand everything
at once to take a useful next step.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.820
Learning with ACA means keeping your own
voice and judgment present while you

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.660
develop new abilities. Confidence grows as
you begin to recognize, I

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.980
understand this better. I can try this. I
know what to check. Thank you for spending

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.060
this time with us. We invite you to begin
your learning journey with ACA.

